# FMOD Studio.
#
# What must be committed: SushiPartyAudio.fspro, Metadata/ and Assets/ (the source
# audio files). Metadata/ is the project's whole object graph — never ignore parts
# of it, or Studio opens with dangling references.

# Local working state
.cache/
.unsaved/
.user/

# --- Built banks ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerate with File > Build in Studio.
#
# The Unity project reads these through `sourceProjectPath`/`sourceBankPath` in
# FMODStudioSettings, so a fresh clone has no audio until someone opens Studio and
# builds once. That is the usual trade: banks are binary, rewritten whole on every
# build, and will grow a lot once real audio replaces the placeholder beeps.
#
# If you would rather a clone just work, delete the line below. Consider Git LFS at
# the same time — `git lfs track "*.bank"`.
/Build/
